<title>CANADA: Manitoba Pool pays C$3.1 mln to retiring farmers.</title>
<headline>Manitoba Pool pays C$3.1 mln to retiring farmers.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-12-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canada's sixth largest grain handler said on Wednesday it will pay a $C3.1 million dividend to 3,200 farmer-members who retire or pass age 65 in 1997.</p>
<p>Manitoba Pool Elevators, a privately held cooperative, makes the payment in December each year.</p>
<p>MPE paid an additional C$269,900 to the estates of deceased members in the past year. The firm has 16,000 farmer members, the annual report said.</p>
<p>MPE reported net earnings of C$5.54 million in fiscal 1995/96 (Aug/July) compared to C$10.05 million the prior year.</p>
<p>((Gilbert Le Gras 204 947 3548))</p>
